WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.355 --> 00:00:03.368
TritonAI Harness is UC San Diego's agent workspace.

2
00:00:03.388 --> 00:00:05.121
It doesn't just answer questions.

3
00:00:05.376 --> 00:00:10.527
It does the work, on your files, with you in control.

4
00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:13.312
Your files stay on your computer.

5
00:00:13.899 --> 00:00:16.573
Only what a task needs goes to an approved model,

6
00:00:16.967 --> 00:00:18.393
through the TritonAI Gateway.

7
00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:22.408
Ask it to summarize a workshop survey.

8
00:00:23.047 --> 00:00:24.222
In Supervised mode,

9
00:00:24.247 --> 00:00:26.587
it checks with you before it runs

10
00:00:26.607 --> 00:00:27.855
a command or changes a file.

11
00:00:28.976 --> 00:00:31.873
About two minutes later, the summary is done,

12
00:00:31.893 --> 00:00:33.866
and every step is logged.

13
00:00:35.983 --> 00:00:37.861
It can also work in desktop apps.

14
00:00:38.084 --> 00:00:39.621
It made this chart in Excel,

15
00:00:39.641 --> 00:00:41.386
using the menus the way you would.

16
00:00:43.485 --> 00:00:46.668
Plugins connect it to the campus systems you already use.

17
00:00:47.302 --> 00:00:49.512
Each ability has its own switch,

18
00:00:49.532 --> 00:00:53.251
and in Supervised mode it asks before it writes anything.

19
00:00:55.366 --> 00:00:59.110
Microsoft 365 reads your Outlook mail and calendar.

20
00:00:59.758 --> 00:01:03.733
Switch on drafts, calendar holds, and Teams chats when you want them.

21
00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.002
It never sends mail for you.

22
00:01:07.124 --> 00:01:12.627
Google Workspace reads your UC San Diego Drive: Docs, Sheets, and Slides.

23
00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:16.569
It finds and summarizes files, but it doesn't change them.

24
00:01:18.663 --> 00:01:21.958
GitHub reviews pull requests, triages issues, and explains failed builds.

25
00:01:22.061 --> 00:01:26.943
It can branch and commit, but it never merges.

26
00:01:27.623 --> 00:01:29.188
That call stays with a person.

27
00:01:30.297 --> 00:01:32.237
Kuali Build shows which forms are in

28
00:01:32.257 --> 00:01:34.180
progress and who they're waiting on.

29
00:01:34.505 --> 00:01:35.792
With writes switched on,

30
00:01:35.837 --> 00:01:36.994
it can start a draft for you

31
00:01:37.014 --> 00:01:38.844
to check before anyone submits it.

32
00:01:39.964 --> 00:01:42.937
And n8n, the campus automation platform, can explain a workflow,

33
00:01:43.163 --> 00:01:44.418
find out why a run failed,

34
00:01:44.615 --> 00:01:48.031
or draft a new one for you to test.

35
00:01:50.154 --> 00:01:52.881
It can turn meeting notes into a slide deck,

36
00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:55.188
on the official UC San Diego template.

37
00:01:57.284 --> 00:02:00.954
You can also build small web apps in the campus style,

38
00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.000
and try them right in the Harness.

39
00:02:04.116 --> 00:02:06.614
Then connect them to campus automation.

40
00:02:07.088 --> 00:02:10.765
This test sign-up ran through every step and saved a new row.

41
00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:18.812
That's TritonAI Harness: real work, on your files, with you in control.
